<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Recife</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mauritsstad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Recife is the capital of the Brazilian state of Pernambuco, a port built on islands and peninsulas where several rivers meet the Atlantic. It grew as the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olinda">Olinda</a> and became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> after 1630, when Johan Maurits of Nassau rebuilt it; the first synagogue in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> opened there. It was the centre of the republican revolts of 1817 and 1824.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/recife.jpg" alt="Recife" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Portal da Copa/ME · CC BY 3.0 br · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antonio_Vaz_island_-_Recife,_Pernambuco,_Brazil_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
